<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Marciano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1554">1554</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Scannagallo · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-war-of-1551-1559">Italian War of 1551–1559</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Marciano, also called Scannagallo, was fought on 2 August 1554 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/val-di-chiana">Valdichiana</a> between the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a> and the Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> and a Franco-Sienese army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piero-strozzi">Piero Strozzi</a>. Strozzi's defeat left Siena isolated, and after a long siege the city surrendered in 1555. Its territory was later granted to Cosimo, a decisive step towards the creation of the Grand Duchy of Tuscany.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marciano.jpg" alt="Battle of Marciano" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giorgio Vasari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giorgio_Vasari_-_The_battle_of_Marciano_in_Val_di_Chiana_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
